KNOWNBUG libstdcxx16
main.cpp
--cpp26
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ S has two data members: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
Static reflection (P2996R13, adopted for C++26 after N5008) through
<meta>: the number of non-static data members of S.  With GCC 16's
headers CBMC fails to parse <type_traits> (`decltype(^^...)').  Needs
GCC 16 -freflection to preprocess (tagged libstdcxx16).
